Comprehensive Slug Utilities Guide

This guide covers the complete slug generation and management system implemented in the Nelson Tech project.

## Overview

The slug utilities provide:
- Universal slug generation for all content types
- Database-backed uniqueness checking
- SEO optimization and validation
- International text support
- Caching for performance
- React hooks for easy integration
- Migration path from legacy utilities

## Quick Start

<code>typescript
import { generateUniqueSlug, useSlugGeneration } from '@/lib/utils';

// Basic usage
const slug = await generateUniqueSlug('My Article Title', 'news');

// In React components
function ArticleForm() {
  const { slug, setSlug, validation, suggestions } = useSlugGeneration(
    title, // source text
    'news', // content type
    { autoGenerate: true }
  );

  return (
    &lt;input 
      value={slug} 
      onChange={(e) =&gt; setSlug(e.target.value)}
      className={validation?.isValid ? 'valid' : 'invalid'}
    /&gt;
  );
}
</code>

## Core Features

### 1. Universal Slug Generation

<code>typescript
import { generateSlug, generateUniqueSlug } from '@/lib/utils/slugUtils';

// Basic slug generation
const slug = generateSlug('Hello World!');
// Result: "hello-world"

// With options
const slug = generateSlug('Café &amp; Restaurant', {
  preserveUnicode: false,
  strict: true,
  maxLength: 30
});
// Result: "cafe-restaurant"

// Database-unique slug
const uniqueSlug = await generateUniqueSlug(
  'My Article Title',
  'news', // content type
  'existing-id', // exclude this ID
  { maxLength: 60 }
);
</code>

### 2. Content Type Support

Supported content types:
- <code>members</code> - User profiles
- <code>companies</code> - Company profiles
- <code>events</code> - Events and workshops
- <code>news</code> - News articles
- <code>opportunities</code> - Job/volunteer opportunities
- <code>groups</code> - Community groups
- <code>resources</code> - Learning resources
- <code>marketplace</code> - Marketplace listings
- <code>pages</code> - Static pages
- <code>topics</code> - Discussion topics

### 3. Advanced Validation

<code>typescript
import { validateSlugSEO, autoFixSlug } from '@/lib/utils/slugValidation';

// Comprehensive validation
const validation = validateSlugSEO('my-article-slug');
if (!validation.isValid) {
  console.log('Errors:', validation.errors);
  console.log('Suggestions:', validation.suggestions);
  console.log('SEO Score:', validation.score); // 0-100
}

// Auto-fix common issues
const { fixedSlug, changesApplied } = autoFixSlug('My--Bad__Slug!');
// Result: { fixedSlug: "my-bad-slug", changesApplied: [...] }
</code>

### 4. Database Lookups

<code>typescript
import { lookupByIdOrSlug, checkSlugExists } from '@/lib/utils/slugUtils';

// Flexible lookup (works with both IDs and slugs)
const { data, foundBy, error } = await lookupByIdOrSlug(
  'my-article-slug', // or UUID
  'news',
  'id,title,slug,created_at' // optional fields
);

// Check availability
const exists = await checkSlugExists('new-slug', 'news', 'exclude-id');
</code>

## React Hooks

### useSlugGeneration

<code>typescript
import { useSlugGeneration } from '@/lib/utils/slugHooks';

function ContentForm({ title, id }) {
  const {
    slug,
    setSlug,
    isGenerating,
    validation,
    suggestions,
    manuallyEdited,
    resetToAutoGeneration,
    applySuggestion,
    autoFix
  } = useSlugGeneration(title, 'news', {
    autoGenerate: true,
    excludeId: id,
    debounceMs: 500
  });

  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
      &lt;input 
        value={slug} 
        onChange={(e) =&gt; setSlug(e.target.value)}
      /&gt;

      {validation &amp;&amp; (
        &lt;div className={validation.isValid ? 'valid' : 'invalid'}&gt;
          Score: {validation.score}/100
          {validation.errors.map(error =&gt; (
            &lt;div key={error} className="error"&gt;{error}&lt;/div&gt;
          ))}
        &lt;/div&gt;
      )}

      {suggestions.length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; (
        &lt;div&gt;
          &lt;h4&gt;Suggestions:&lt;/h4&gt;
          {suggestions.map(suggestion =&gt; (
            &lt;button 
              key={suggestion}
              onClick={() =&gt; applySuggestion(suggestion)}
            &gt;
              {suggestion}
            &lt;/button&gt;
          ))}
        &lt;/div&gt;
      )}

      &lt;button onClick={autoFix}&gt;Auto-fix Issues&lt;/button&gt;
      &lt;button onClick={resetToAutoGeneration}&gt;Reset to Auto&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}
</code>

### useSlugLookup

<code>typescript
import { useSlugLookup } from '@/lib/utils/slugHooks';

function ContentViewer({ identifier }) {
  const { data, loading, error, foundBy, refetch } = useSlugLookup(
    identifier,
    'news',
    'id,title,content,slug'
  );

  if (loading) return &lt;div&gt;Loading...&lt;/div&gt;;
  if (error) return &lt;div&gt;Error: {error}&lt;/div&gt;;
  if (!data) return &lt;div&gt;Not found&lt;/div&gt;;

  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
      &lt;h1&gt;{data.title}&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;Found by: {foundBy}&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;div&gt;{data.content}&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}
</code>

### useSlugAvailability

<code>typescript
import { useSlugAvailability } from '@/lib/utils/slugHooks';

function SlugChecker({ slug, contentType }) {
  const { isAvailable, checking } = useSlugAvailability(slug, contentType);

  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
      {checking ? (
        &lt;span&gt;Checking...&lt;/span&gt;
      ) : isAvailable === true ? (
        &lt;span className="available"&gt;✓ Available&lt;/span&gt;
      ) : isAvailable === false ? (
        &lt;span className="taken"&gt;✗ Already taken&lt;/span&gt;
      ) : null}
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}
</code>

## Performance Features

### Caching

<code>typescript
import { slugCacheUtils } from '@/lib/utils/slugUtils';

// Cache management
slugCacheUtils.clearAll();
slugCacheUtils.clearForContentType('news');
slugCacheUtils.preloadSlugs('news', 100);

const stats = slugCacheUtils.getStats();
console.log(`Cache size: ${stats.size}`);
</code>

### Batch Operations

<code>typescript
import { generateMultipleSlugs } from '@/lib/utils/slugUtils';

const items = [
  { text: 'First Article', id: '1' },
  { text: 'Second Article', id: '2' },
  { text: 'Third Article', id: '3' }
];

const results = await generateMultipleSlugs(items, 'news');
// Results include unique slugs for each item
</code>

## SEO Optimization

The utilities include comprehensive SEO optimization:

### Automatic Improvements
- Remove stop words ("the", "and", "of", etc.)
- Optimize length for search engines
- Handle international characters
- Prevent reserved word conflicts
- Score slugs for SEO quality (0-100)

### Best Practices
<code>typescript
// Good slugs
"ultimate-guide-react-hooks"      // Score: 95
"javascript-tips-beginners"       // Score: 90
"web-development-tools"           // Score: 85

// Poor slugs
"the-ultimate-guide-to-the-best"  // Score: 45 (too many stop words)
"a"                               // Score: 20 (too short)
"very-very-long-slug-with-many"   // Score: 30 (too long)
</code>

## Migration Guide

### From Legacy Utilities

<code>typescript
// Old way (deprecated)
import { generateSlug } from '@/utils/slugUtils';
const slug = generateSlug('My Title');

// New way
import { generateSlug } from '@/lib/utils/slugUtils';
const slug = generateSlug('My Title', { strict: true });

// With database uniqueness
import { generateUniqueSlug } from '@/lib/utils/slugUtils';
const uniqueSlug = await generateUniqueSlug('My Title', 'news');
</code>

