## Configuration

### Environment-Specific Settings

<code>typescript
// Development: More permissive
const devOptions = {
  strict: false,
  maxLength: 200,
  allowUppercase: true
};

// Production: Strict SEO
const prodOptions = {
  strict: true,
  maxLength: 80,
  allowUppercase: false
};
</code>

### Content Type Customization

<code>typescript
// Customize per content type
const newsOptions = {
  maxLength: 80,
  removeStopWords: true,
  includeDate: false
};

const eventOptions = {
  maxLength: 70,
  removeStopWords: false,
  includeDate: true
};
</code>

## Error Handling

<code>typescript
try {
  const slug = await generateUniqueSlug('My Title', 'news');
} catch (error) {
  if (error.message.includes('Could not generate unique slug')) {
    // Handle uniqueness failure
    console.error('Too many similar slugs exist');
  } else {
    // Handle other errors
    console.error('Slug generation failed:', error);
  }
}
</code>

## Testing

<code>typescript
import { generateSlug, validateSlugSEO } from '@/lib/utils';

describe('Slug utilities', () =&gt; {
  test('generates SEO-friendly slugs', () =&gt; {
    const slug = generateSlug('My Test Article!');
    expect(slug).toBe('my-test-article');

    const validation = validateSlugSEO(slug);
    expect(validation.isValid).toBe(true);
    expect(validation.score).toBeGreaterThan(80);
  });
});
</code>

## Best Practices

1. Always use content types for database uniqueness
2. Enable auto-generation in forms for better UX
3. Validate slugs before saving to database
4. Cache frequently accessed slugs for performance
5. Use batch operations for bulk updates
6. Handle internationalization with unicode support
7. Monitor SEO scores to maintain quality
8. Test edge cases like very long titles

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

**Slug generation fails**
<code>typescript
// Check if text is valid
if (!text || typeof text !== 'string') {
  throw new Error('Invalid text provided');
}
</code>

**Database lookup fails**
<code>typescript
// Verify content type configuration
if (!CONTENT_TYPE_CONFIG[contentType]) {
  throw new Error(`Unsupported content type: ${contentType}`);
}
</code>

**Cache not working**
<code>typescript
// Clear and reinitialize cache
slugCacheUtils.clearAll();
await slugCacheUtils.preloadSlugs('news', 100);
</code>

### Performance Tips

1. Preload common slugs during app initialization
2. Use debouncing in form inputs (500ms recommended)
3. Batch operations when processing multiple items
4. Monitor cache hit rates and adjust TTL as needed
5. Use appropriate content type limits for slug length

This comprehensive slug system provides everything needed for professional URL management with excellent performance, SEO optimization, and developer experience.
